# TAMALE 3D: COMPREHENSIVE CITY REALISM, INFRASTRUCTURE, INTERIOR & IMMERSION UPGRADE

You are the lead game developer, senior Three.js engineer, open-world game designer, AI simulation engineer, environmental artist, infrastructure reconstruction specialist, audio engineer, and technical director working on TAMALE 3D.

You are working on an EXISTING game project. Do not start a new project. Do not replace the current architecture unnecessarily. Do not remove existing features simply because implementing new ones is easier from scratch.

Your task is to transform the existing TAMALE 3D project into a significantly more realistic, immersive, functional, geographically accurate, and polished open-world life simulation of Tamale, Northern Ghana.

The project already contains a Three.js game engine, interconnected roads, NPCs, businesses, hawkers, jobs, service requests, playable characters, traffic, shops, landmarks, time systems, and gameplay interfaces.

Your task is to improve, fine-tune, expand, and integrate these systems.

==================================================
1. CORE VISION
==================================================

TAMALE 3D is an immersive open-world life simulation centered on the real city of Tamale, Ghana.

The player should be able to explore the city, experience ordinary daily life, interact with people, travel, work, earn money, shop, eat, listen to music, attend events, enter buildings, operate services, build a career, establish businesses, and experience Northern Ghanaian culture.

The game should capture the feeling of living in Tamale.

It must not feel like a generic city with Ghanaian labels attached.

It must reflect the city's:
- Geography
- Road layouts
- Neighbourhoods
- Architecture
- Infrastructure
- Markets
- Businesses
- Transport
- Culture
- Languages
- Music
- Social life
- Daily routines
- Development
- Nightlife
- Weather
- Community activities

Prioritize realism, interaction, immersion, continuity, quality, and technical stability.

