- Load or activate the correct interior.
- Place the player inside at the appropriate entrance.
- Prevent camera clipping.
- Prevent falling through floors.
- Preserve the correct active character.

When the player exits:
- Return them to the correct exterior building entrance.
- Restore the correct orientation.
- Preserve the world state.
- Preserve time progression.
- Preserve NPC and traffic state as appropriate.

Avoid abrupt black-screen teleportation where a seamless door transition is technically achievable.

If interior loading requires a transition, make it short, polished, and immersive.

Do not create separate disconnected interiors that have no logical relationship to the building outside.

